d 'CROSSWALK_MULTICLASS': module to provide crosswalk tables to translate ISCO-88com and ISCO-08 into the Multilevel Socio-Economic Classes schemes
d
d  crosswalk_multiclass is an add-on for the crosswalk package (Ben
d Jann). It provides crosswalk tables translating ISCO-88com and
d ISCO-08 occupational codes into the Multilevel Socio-Economic
d Classes (MSEC) schemes -- Micro-SEC (30 classes), Meso-SEC (18
d classes), and Macro-SEC (11 classes, ESEC plus differentiation of
d SC I and II) -- plus, for ISCO-08 only, a separate 77-category
d micro-class scheme that is not part of MSEC. Micro-SEC, Meso-SEC
d and Macro-SEC are defined jointly over occupation and employment
d relation, so those tables carry one destination column per
d employment status; two case functions are supplied to build that
d argument, either from a self-employment indicator and a
d supervisory/employee-count variable, or from a status variable
d already coded 1-5. The micro-class scheme is purely occupational
d and takes no case argument. Tables are provided for 4-digit ISCO
d codes and, directly, for 3-digit ISCO minor groups. The MSEC
d schemes nest: Micro-SEC, Meso-SEC and Macro-SEC each aggregate to
d the European Socio-economic Classification (ESeC). This package
d does not duplicate plain ESeC itself, since crosswalk already
d provides isco88_to_esec() and isco08_to_esec(); see help
d crosswalk_multiclass for details and the correct case functions
d to use with them. The package contains no ado-file and defines no
d command of its own; all recoding is carried out by crosswalk. 
d
d KW: ISCO
d KW: occupation
d KW: social class
d KW: ESeC
d KW: Macro-SEC
d KW: micro-class
d KW: Meso-SEC
d KW: Micro-SEC
d KW: MSEC
d KW: class scheme
d KW: crosswalk
d KW: recode
d
d Requires: Stata version 14 and crosswalk, moremata from SSC (q.v.)
d
d Distribution-Date: 20260825
d
d Author: Oscar Smallenbroek,  European Commission
d Support: email Oscar.SMALLENBROEK@@ec.europa.eu
d
f crosswalk_multiclass.sthlp
